language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ csplib_033_word_design: an Essence' model from DCP Rosetta.
$
$ Find a set of num_words words of length n over the alphabet {A, C, G, T} such that each word has 4 symbols from {C, G}, each pair of distinct words differs in at least 4 positions, and for each pair of words x and y in the set (where x and y may be identical), the reverse of x and the Watson-Crick complement of y differ in at least 4 positions. The Watson-Crick complement replaces each A by T and each C by G, and vice versa.
$
$ Save this file as model.eprime. Download `csplib_033_word_design.json` and `dcp_convert_essence.py` from the
$ problem's page:
$   https://dcp-bench.github.io/DCP-Rosetta/problems/csplib_033_word_design.html
$ Convert the instances once, then run the first one with Savile Row 1.11 (it needs Java); the
$ solution is written to `csplib_033_word_design_1.param.solution`:
$   python dcp_convert_essence.py csplib_033_word_design.json
$   savilerow model.eprime csplib_033_word_design_1.param -run-solver

$ n: length of each word
given n : int(1..)
$ num_words: number of words in the set
given num_words : int(1..)

$ the letters, coded 1 to 4
letting A = 1
letting C = 2
letting G = 3
letting T = 4
$ the minimum number of positions in which two words must differ
letting MIN_DIFF = 4

$ words[i,j]: letter j of word i (indices 1-based, letters coded A=1, C=2, G=3, T=4)
find words : matrix indexed by [int(1..num_words), int(1..n)] of int(1..4)

branching on [words]
such that
$ each word has 4 symbols from {C, G}
forAll i : int(1..num_words) . ((sum j : int(1..n) . toInt(words[i,j] = C \/ words[i,j] = G)) = 4),
$ each pair of distinct words differs in at least 4 positions
forAll i : int(1..num_words) . forAll i2 : int(i+1..num_words) . ((sum j : int(1..n) . toInt(words[i,j] != words[i2,j])) >= MIN_DIFF),
$ the reverse of each word and the Watson-Crick complement of each word (including a word with itself) differ in at least 4 positions; the complement of letter v is 5-v (A<->T, C<->G)
forAll i : int(1..num_words) . forAll i2 : int(1..num_words) . ((sum j : int(1..n) . toInt(words[i,n+1-j] != 5 - words[i2,j])) >= MIN_DIFF)
